{
  "summary": "Turns the `building-on` triplet evaluation in `contrib/guix/toolchains.scm` from a top-level variable evaluated at module load time into a procedure. This ensures derivations evaluate their `--build` triplet dynamically under the system specified by `--system` rather than locking in the host system.",
  "problem": "When running Guix under foreign architectures (for example, building for `aarch64-linux` on an `x86_64` host using emulation), `guix shell` loads manifests before applying `--system`. `building-on` therefore captures the host architecture, configuring cross-toolchain packages like `gcc-cross-sans-libc` with mismatched `--build` triplets and causing configure-time failures.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: `gcc-cross-sans-libc` fails to configure with `checking for CET support... configure: error: compiler and assembler with CET support are required for --enable-cet` when running `--system=aarch64-linux` on an x86_64 host",
    "PR description: author verified that native builds produce identical derivations on master and with this PR, leaving standard release builds unchanged"
  ],
