  "scope_notes": "Small 4-line Guile Scheme adjustment in Guix toolchain manifests.",
  "changed_since_previous": "",
  "card": "Turns the Guix `building-on` triplet resolution in `contrib/guix/toolchains.scm` into a procedure evaluated per derivation rather than at module load time. When running Guix with `--system` on a host of a different architecture (such as via emulation), Guix manifests previously locked in the host system triplet, causing cross-compiler packages like `gcc-cross-sans-libc` to fail configuration. The change enables cross-architecture Guix container builds while leaving derivations for native release builds identical.",
